<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">follow me like the moon</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;It's 1980s London, and ballerina Catra's miserable until Welsh country girl Adora stumbles into her dance class. Yet what seems like a harmless flirtation quickly turns her life inside out.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sequel alternative POV to my fic 'she walks me through the night' - you'll need to read this first! Light 1980s angst with a happy ending inspired by yet another brilliant Sammy Rae &amp;amp; The Friends' track, the eponymous 'Follow Me Like the Moon'.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;---&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Catra never thought sheâ€™d be so turned on by a Welsh accent, but it turns out sheâ€™s discovering new things about herself everyday. Sheâ€™s too slow to react though - the lead instructor catches her eye, and Catra realises theyâ€™re already running late. Sheâ€™ll have to be quick.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;â€œNothing wrong with your arse,â€ Catra smirks when her voice makes the blonde startle, brushing past her purposefully as she makes her way to the front of the class, â€œPosture is another story, though.â€&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Catra knows she doesnâ€™t need to stretch - sheâ€™s certainly not going to do anything strenuous teaching a beginnerâ€™s class - but she canâ€™t resist showing off a little now she knows sheâ€™s got that girlâ€™s attention. If thereâ€™s anything Catra knows how to do, itâ€™s tease.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
